    "observed_text": "EURUSD and USDJPY: two falling quotes, two dollar directions\n\nWhy it matters: The first chart puts both relationships into currency units per dollar and measures their change from October 26. For the euro, that requires taking the reciprocal of EURUSD; the yen quote already measures what one dollar buys. On this basis, the dollar ended October 30 up 0.13% against the euro and down 0.07% against the yen. The inverted euro rate is calculated from the Fed quote.\n\nContext: Euro- or yen-specific policy expectations and demand for safer assets could outweigh the US yield channel. The October 26-30 Fed reference-rate comparison cannot identify which driver dominated.\n\nRead the full brief: https://lnkd.in/gtmeWj4W\n\nAnalysis, not financial advice. Readers decide whether to trade.\n\nCapital Chronicle may hold positions in the markets it covers.",
